hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1505","Ismail bin Musa Al-Fazari told us, Ibrahim, meaning Ibn Saad, told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Salamah, and Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “When the prayer is established, do not perform it while you are striving; perform it.” As you walk, be at ease. Pray for whatever you catch up with, and make up for what you miss.”"
